Acute Myocardial Infarction - Ruled out/unlikely due to: Nausea and tachycardia clearly correlating with acute panic rather than ischemic chest pain, and entirely normal oxygen saturation.

Peptic Ulcer Disease - Ruled out/unlikely due to: Absence of localized epigastric point tenderness and negative history of NSAID overuse.
